Subject: wined3d: do delayed clears inside the current Vulkan render pass
Date: 2026-10-15
Applies to: CrossOver 26.3.0 Wine sources, after 0012
Files changed: dlls/wined3d/context_vk.c, dlls/wined3d/wined3d_vk.h

A full clear is delayed until the next draw, which then begins a render pass
that clears on load. If a render pass was already running on the same views,
wined3d ended it and began a new one just for the clear. BO1 clears like this
about 170 times per frame in busy scenes, so about 90% of its render passes
(up to about 200 per frame) were restarts on the same attachments, and Apple's
tile-based GPUs store and reload every attachment at each one. When the view
is attached to the running pass and covers its render area, it is now cleared
with vkCmdClearAttachments inside the pass.

Test: tools/d3d9-clear-test.c
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like the Wine files it modifies.
---
--- a/dlls/wined3d/context_vk.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/context_vk.c
